&key parameters should validate the form of the &rest argument list:
it should be a list of even length, and it should contain a SYMBOL at
even indexed positions. If &allow-other-keys is not specified
(careful, there are two ways to specify it, one in the lambda-list,
the other in the parameter list :allow-other-keys t) Basically it
should be a p-list with symbols as keys.

("~/src/lisp/encours/symbol-sxhash.fas") is not a valid &rest argument list for &key.
(:output-file "/tmp/symbol-sxhash.fas") is a valid &rest argument list for &key.


compile-file should signal an error instead of ignoring the invalid argument:
but I guess the problem impacts all &key functions.

