----------------------------------------------------------------------
DONE (slice 48, v1.1.5) — issue resolved, moved to issues/closed.
&KEY argument lists are now validated in the kernel lambda-list binder
(bind_required_parameters, sources/eval.c), for every &KEY function and macro:
  - the keyword-argument portion must be a PROPER LIST of EVEN length;
  - every key (even index) must be a SYMBOL;
  - unless other keys are allowed — &ALLOW-OTHER-KEYS in the lambda list, or
    :ALLOW-OTHER-KEYS with a non-NIL value in the call — every key must name one
    of the declared &KEY parameters (:ALLOW-OTHER-KEYS itself is always accepted).
Violations signal a PROGRAM-ERROR (new program_error()/PROGRAM_ERROR in
sources/boerror.c, signalling PROGRAM_ERROR_Class so HANDLER-CASE can catch it).
The declared keywords are accumulated during binding (rooted across init-form
evaluation); &REST + &KEY and &KEY + &AUX combinations validate correctly.

Verified: the issue's exact case (compile-file "x.lisp" "x.fas") — where the
positional "x.fas" was silently swallowed as a bad &rest plist — now signals a
PROGRAM-ERROR; valid (compile-file "x.lisp" :output-file "x.fas") still works;
unknown key / odd length / non-symbol key all raise PROGRAM-ERROR;
:allow-other-keys t and &allow-other-keys suppress the unknown-key check;
make-array/make-hash-table/sort/remove/find/reduce &KEY calls unaffected.
